`permutation_familywise_separation_auc` tests trajectory separation over a family of results (such as one per frequency band, built from the same trials) and several contrasts. Each permutation relabels trials inside caller-chosen `strata`, so only the tested factor moves, and applies the relabelling to every result; one strata row per contrast draws one relabelling per contrast. Each (result, contrast) is standardised by its own null before the maximum (`standardize=True`), so results on different scales weigh equally; the table gives family-wise p-values, and the per-member null AUCs are returned. `permutation_null_separation_auc` takes `strata` in place of `within_subject`, returns `(observed, null, p_value)`, and keeps every permutation. Both raise when an AUC is NaN, when a stratum leaves trials of a contrast unable to change group (naming the strata), or when a null has zero spread, and take `per_subject=True` to average the subjects' separation curves instead of separating pooled trials. `permute_labels_within_strata` moved to `coco_pipe.utils` so decoding and dim_reduction share it; `coco_pipe.decoding` still exports it.
